(Title) Tj
T*
(Prenatal Aerobic Exercise Reduces Postpartum Depression: Findings From a Randomized) Tj
T*
(Controlled Trial of Pregnant Women) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Physical activity during pregnancy may confer psychological benefits that extend into the) Tj
T*
(postpartum period. We randomized 398 pregnant women with uncomplicated pregnancies to) Tj
T*
(either structured aerobic exercise \(three 60-minute sessions weekly through mid-gestation\)) Tj
T*
(or routine prenatal care. At three months postpartum, women in the exercise group) Tj
T*
(exhibited substantially lower depressive symptom scores on validated instruments compared) Tj
T*
(to the standard-care group. The proportion of women meeting screening criteria for) Tj
T*
(possible postpartum depression was significantly reduced in the exercise group. Clinical) Tj
T*
(diagnoses of postpartum depression were correspondingly lower in the active group.) Tj
T*
(Maternal and neonatal outcomes including gestational complications, delivery method, and) Tj
T*
(neonatal health indicators were similar between groups, indicating the exercise) Tj
T*
(intervention was safe. These findings support incorporating aerobic physical activity into) Tj
T*
(prenatal care as a practical, accessible strategy to reduce postpartum depressive symptoms) Tj
T*
(and promote maternal mental health in low-risk pregnancies.) Tj
ET
